  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Consider the bcc unit cells of the solids <math><mn>1</mn></math> and <math><mn>2</mn></math> with the position of atoms as shown below. The radius of atom <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi></math> is twice that of atom <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The unit cell edge length is <math><mn>50</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">%</mi></math> more in solid <math><mn>2</mn></math> than in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math> . What is the approximate packing efficiency in solid <math><mn>2</mn></math> ?</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/35e09cc0-d31d-4f83-9e71-0c32fc6b936c-image.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 210px;\" /></p>",
    "image": null
